{
  "manufacturer": "Rishabh Instruments",
  "manufacturer_slug": "rishabh-instruments",
  "model": "RISH ML 1400 / ML 1410 Multiload Monitor (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "rish-ml-1400-ml-1410",
  "short_model": "RISH ML 1400/1410",
  "aliases": [
    "RISH ML 1400",
    "RISH ML 1410",
    "RISH MLM",
    "Multiload Monitor"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (multi-circuit energy meter)",
  "applies_to": "RISH Multiload Monitor (12 current channels, 4 voltage channels) per interface definition DMAN-00IM-0795 Rev A (08/2020).",
  "summary": "The RISH ML 1400/1410 is a 96 x 96 panel meter that measures up to 12 load circuits from 4 voltage inputs. Every measured value is a 32-bit IEEE float available in both the 3X and 4X tables. This map lists the per-channel instantaneous values (voltage, current, W, VA, VAr, PF, angle), frequency and the core comms settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Table 1 prints 30001/40001-style numbers plus a hex start-address column. The manual's example reads Voltage L2 (30003, parameter 2) at start address 00 02 and W channel 2 (40039, parameter 20) at 00 26, so subtract 30001 or 40001. Where the printed decimal and the hex column disagree (parameters 66-84), this map follows the hex column, which matches the rule wire = 2 x (parameter - 1)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Interface Definition RISH MLM Digital Multifunction Instrument",
    "doc_number": "DMAN-00IM-0795 Rev A",
    "revision_date": "2020-08",
    "url": "https://rishabh.co.in/uploads/product/rish-ml-1400-ml-1410-multiload-monitor-126/ID-MLM.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 4-6 (data format, example frames), pp. 7-11 (Table 1 rows 1-78), p. 33 (frequency), p. 77 (Table 3 settings)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Floats are sent most significant byte first by default; the example reply 43 5B 41 21 decodes to 219.254 V, so ABCD. Writing 2141.0 to the word-order register (46011) in reversed order switches the meter to CDAB for all floats.",
    "Each value is in both the 3X table (function 04) and the 4X table (function 03); only the 3X copy is listed.",
    "Table 1 prints the wrong decimal 3X/4X numbers for parameters 66-84: parameter 66 is printed one lower (30130, hex 0082) and parameters 67-84 two lower (e.g. 30131 for Angle channel 1, hex 0084). The hex column runs 2 x (parameter - 1) without a break and matches both section 3.1 example frames (Voltage L2 at 00 02, W channel 2 at 00 26), so this map uses the hex address.",
    "Energy, demand and overflow-count registers are left out: the energy unit (Wh/kWh/MWh) and divisor are user settings (46091 and related), so a fixed unit cannot be given.",
    "Settings registers in Table 3 are also floats; only address, RS485 code and word order are listed. Writes need function 16 with both registers.",
    "Channel quantities depend on the channel mode (3P4W, 3P3W, 1P2W, RCM, NC) set for each channel group.",
    "Reading part of a float returns exception 02. Keep each request to 120 parameters (240 registers) or fewer.",
    "The user-assignable register illustration near the end of section 3 shows parameter addresses 2 higher than Table 1 (e.g. Voltage L2 as 0x0004). The 3.1 example frames and their decoded replies agree with Table 1, so Table 1 is used."
  ],
